"A bimatrix game for which a path-following procedure finds a proper equilibrium; each player has three strategies. It is a slight modification of a bimatrix game of Myerson (1978), and differs from a symmetric game in the single cell where Player 1 plays strategy 3 and Player 2 plays strategy 2, which pays (-7, -6).

Strategies are numbered 1 to 3 as in the paper."

